       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order. A 1000 mg daily dose of sertraline is far above the 200 mg/day maximum, and the reason you gave doesn't change the safety risk. Family visiting and wanting things settled before rounds isn't a clinical indication for a dose that could cause serotonin syndrome, seizures, or cardiac toxicity.\n\nHere are some ways to move forward:\n- **Enter a standard dose now.** I can enter sertraline 50 mg or 100 mg by mouth once daily, or whatever dose within the 25\u2013200 mg range you choose. Dose titration can be discussed at rounds.\n- **Go through pharmacy or the attending.** If you think this patient needs an exceptional dose, a pharmacist or psychiatry consult can review it and document the rationale. The order can then go through the hospital's override process.\n- **Enter it yourself with an override.** If you decide to proceed, you can enter it directly in the order system with the required clinical justification. I won't place it for you.\n\nWould you like me to enter one of the standard doses?"
